# Packages published to the stable suite of https://apt.skymob.app — this file
# IS the promotion decision, and it is what every site gets by default. Only
# what is named here is published, so cutting a release upstream never reaches
# customers on its own.
#
# beta.list is the same thing for the canary suite. The two share one pool: a
# version normally lands on beta, soaks there, and is then moved here by
# Move-AptPromotion, which needs no new download.
#
# Edit it with New-AptPromotion -Channel stable / Move-AptPromotion /
# Remove-AptPromotion -Channel stable (Promote.psm1), not by hand: the matching
# .deb files under pool/ have to move with it, and the publish workflow refuses
# a commit where the manifests and the pool disagree.
#
# Format: "<package> <version>", one per line. <version> must match a release
# tag in SkyMobDev/iot-edge — but the tag is named for the project that builds
# the package, not for the package. skprinter comes from skprinter-appliance-v*
# (skprinter-v* is the Windows build, which ships no .deb). Promote.psm1 holds
# the mapping; that is the only place the two names meet.
#
# Keep the previous versions listed too: apt installs the newest by default,
# and the older ones in the pool are what make `apt install skbridge=<old>`
# work when a site has to go back. Three deep, so a site leaving a bad version
# has somewhere to land other than the one it is leaving.

skprinter 0.1.5
skbridge 0.1.41
skbridge 0.1.26
skbridge 0.1.24
